-### [Uncertainty Prediction Loss](2961-uncertainty-prediction-loss.md)
-Uncertainty Prediction Loss is a regularization technique used in differentiable volume rendering and neural radiance field optimization to predict and penalize the aleatoric uncertainty of rendered outputs or geometric fields. It differs from standard photometric losses by explicitly modeling the confidence of the prediction, allowing the optimizer to down-weight noisy or ambiguous data points. Unlike [Uniform and Gaussian Noise Models](5127-uniform-and-gaussian-noise-regularization.md), which visualize uncertainty distributions, this method directly incorporates uncertainty parameters into the training objective to improve geometry and color reconstruction.
-
 ### [Data Consistency Loss](2976-data-consistency-loss.md)
 Data Consistency Loss minimizes the discrepancy between the forward-projected scene representation and the measured input data, ensuring the optimized volume adheres to physical observations. It differs from sibling methods like [Total Variation Regularization](860-total-variation-regularization.md) or [Perceptual Loss Training](2000-perceptual-loss-training.md) by operating directly in the measurement domain (e.g., projection space or raw pixel values) rather than relying solely on spatial smoothness or high-level feature similarity.
