 ### TensoRF Reconstruction Optimization
-#### definition
-- [S5, unofficial] Optimizing the tensorial radiance field per scene via gradient descent to minimize L2 rendering loss, using ground truth pixel colors as supervision.
-#### step
-- [S5, unofficial] Initialize tensor factors (global vectors and matrices).
-- [S5, unofficial] Compute rendering loss (L2) between rendered pixel colors and ground truth pixel colors.
-- [S5, unofficial] Apply regularization terms to vector and matrix factors to address overfitting and local minima.
-- [S5, unofficial] Apply coarse-to-fine reconstruction by linearly and bilinearly upsampling XYZ-mode vector and matrix factors at specific optimization steps.
-#### parameter
-- [S5, unofficial] L1 norm loss: Sparsity loss applied to factors. Used for most datasets.
-- [S5, unofficial] TV (Total Variation) loss: Applied for real datasets with few input images (e.g., LLFF) or imperfect capture conditions (e.g., Tanks and Temples with varying exposure/inconsistent masks).
-- [S5, unofficial] Upsampling Steps: 2000, 3000, 4000, 5500, 7000.
-- [S5, unofficial] Initial Resolution: N0^3 voxels with N0 = 128.
-- [S5, unofficial] Final Resolution: N^3 voxels. Interpolation between N0^3 and N^3 is linear in logarithmic space.
